  ('bavaria-germany', '01F', 'Bavaria', 'Germany', 'Beer halls and fairy-tale castles, alpine lakes and medieval', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Bavaria & the Alpine South', '{"culture","entertainment","wellness","family","culinary","ski"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Germany''s largest + most-visited state; Munich = capital + node FLAGSHIP + base","Own hub content = the Bavarian Lakes: Chiemsee (Schloss Herrenchiemsee), Starnberger See, Tegernsee","Castles + Alps along the south (Neuschwanstein, Zugspitze 2,962m, Berchtesgaden/Konigssee)","Franconia''s old towns north (Nuremberg, Bamberg, Regensburg, Rothenburg/Romantic Road)","Bavaria-Austria seam: Berchtesgaden in this node; Salzburg in the Austria node (cross-link, no double-cover)","26M overnight stays 2023 (~20.6% national); Upper Bavaria ~40M, a third in Munich","Oktoberfest ~6.5M visitors / ~6.5M litres 2025 (record ~7.2M in 2023); Theresienwiese; 19 Sep-4 Oct 2026","Neuschwanstein ~1.3M visitors/yr (up to 6,000/day summer), begun 1869 by Ludwig II; UNESCO inscription 12 Jul 2025 (Ludwig II palaces serial property, Germany''s 55th site)","German Alpine Road (Deutsche Alpenstrasse) ~484 km Lindau-to-Konigssee; 20+ lakes, 60+ villages, the region''s scenic through-line","Chiemsee ~80 km2 (max 73.4 m, Germany''s 3rd-largest); Herreninsel 238 ha (Herrenchiemsee, begun 1878) + Fraueninsel 15.5 ha; Prien ~57 min from Munich","Reinheitsgebot (Beer Purity Law) adopted 23 Apr 1516 — among the world''s oldest food laws still in force; Bavaria/Franconia = Europe''s densest brewery country","Nuremberg Christkindlesmarkt ~2M visitors/yr, 180+ stalls, first recorded 1530; Advent tentpole of Bavaria''s December","Ski picture: Zugspitze glacier (~2,600-2,720 m, Germany''s highest pistes) + Allgau/Oberstdorf (Nebelhorn 2,224 m, Germany''s longest run ~7.5 km; Fellhorn/Kanzelwand ~36 km cross-border) — each town its own dossier","Konigssee (Berchtesgaden) ~190 m deep, Germany''s cleanest lake; electric-only boats since 1909 (19 wooden boats) to St. Bartholoma (founded 1134) under the Watzmann — own dossier","Romantic Road (Romantische Strasse) ~460 km Wurzburg-to-Fussen, 29 official stops incl. Rothenburg ob der Tauber (Germany''s best-preserved walled town) — own dossier","Wieskirche near Steingaden: oval Rococo pilgrimage church (completed 1754, Zimmermann brothers), UNESCO since 1983, 1M+ visitors/yr","Munich''s Englischer Garten: 375 ha (laid out from 1789), one of the world''s largest inner-city parks; Chinesischer Turm beer garden ~7,000 seats (own dossier)","Bamberg UNESCO old town (1993): ~13 breweries in town / ~240 in region (Germany''s densest); Schlenkerla Rauchbier since 1405 (own dossier)","Chiemsee formed ~10,000 years ago (once ~240 km2, 3x today''s size); among Bavaria''s cleanest bathing lakes","Bavaria UNESCO density: Ludwig II palaces (2025), Wieskirche (1983), Regensburg old town (2006), Bamberg old town (1993), Roman Limes"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 (fire/ambulance/medical) / 110 (police); Bergwacht + Wasserwacht via 112","hospital":"Munich (LMU Klinikum / Munchen Klinik) regional hub; each satellite lists local","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","note":"lakes = sudden alpine-foehn storms (heed harbour flags) + early-season cold-shock; alpine spine in satellite dossiers","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/germany","read":"2026-08-20T14:48:19Z","page_updated":"2026-08-11T10:18:05+01:00","source_country":"germany","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"peak":"Oktoberfest 19 Sep-4 Oct 2026 overflow + Jun-Aug + Dec markets","shoulder":"May-Jun + late Sep/Oct","green":"Nov + Jan-Mar (ex-ski/markets)","booking_lead":"Oktoberfest 6-12 mo; summer 2-4 mo; ski 3-6 mo; markets 3-5 mo","off_season_specials":"Nov + Jan-Mar lake-spa/city/ski; year-round ca