  ('berchtesgaden-konigssee-germany', '01F', 'Berchtesgaden & the Königssee', 'Germany', 'An emerald fjord-lake under the Watzmann', 'live', 'verified', 'desertDunes', 'Bavaria & the Alpine South', '{"adventure","culture","romance","family","ski","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Konigssee = electric-boat-only lake; St. Bartholoma stop ~35 min + Salet/Obersee in full season; boatman''s echo-trumpet","Watzmann massif + Berchtesgaden National Park (Germany''s only alpine national park)","Salzbergwerk = Germany''s oldest active salt mine (miners'' train + slide + underground salt lake by boat + salt cathedral)","Dokumentation Obersalzberg reopened 27 Sep 2023 (''Idyll and Crime''; 2025 Luigi Micheletti Award) — memorial + education at a Nazi perpetrator site","Kehlsteinhaus (''Eagle''s Nest'') by special bus + tunnel elevator; somber-history building, viewpoint/restaurant; closed in winter","Full lake service ~mid-May-mid-Oct (to Salet); winter to St. Bartholoma only","Kempinski Hotel Berchtesgaden 5-star (two-Michelin-star PUR); ~30 min from Salzburg","Konigssee 7.7 km long, up to 190 m deep (Germany''s 3rd-deepest), 603 m elevation; ''cleanest lake in Germany'' — electric-only boats since 1909","Watzmann Mittelspitze 2,713 m (Germany''s 3rd-highest, highest wholly-German peak); East Face ~1,800 m vertical = longest wall in the Eastern Alps","Berchtesgaden National Park est. 1 Aug 1978, ~210 km2 — the only national park in the German Alps","Obersee (past Salet) + Rothbachfall = Germany''s highest waterfall at 470 m (foot access only via Fischunkelalm)","Salzbergwerk founded 1517 (oldest active salt mine in Germany); ~1 hr tour, miners'' train ~650 m in, constant 12 C","Kehlsteinhaus on the 1,834 m Kehlstein; 6.5 km road blasted in 13 months + 124 m tunnel to a brass elevator; 8 electric buses (41 seats) since 2023; road closed all winter (avalanche)","Jenner: modern glass-gondola Jennerbahn to 1,800 m summit; NO groomed pistes — freeride/ski-route/toboggan/winter hiking + DSV base","Konigssee bobsleigh/luge/skeleton track (Schonau) = world''s first artificial-ice track (1968), 1,640 m, 18 curves; flood-damaged Jul 2021, not reopening for competition until Nov 2026","Watzmann Therme brine spa: 900 m2 water, 32 C salt pools (2-3% brine), 80 m slide, daily 10:00-22:00","Kempinski Hotel Berchtesgaden: 138 rooms at ~1,000 m, 1,400 m2 spa, two-Michelin-star PUR + Johann Grill","Ramsau St. Sebastian church (Malerwinkel) + Hintersee + Zauberwald = one of Bavaria''s most-photographed painters'' scenes","Avalanche: Lawinenwarndienst Bayern publishes next-day bulletin from 18:00 (German+English), 5-level scale, 10 Bavarian sub-regions, 19 measuring stations","Wimbachklamm gorge (Ramsau): ~200 m boardwalk through Dachstein limestone, open to visitors since 1847, ~150,000 visitors/yr, ~1 May-1 Nov, ~EUR 4","Rossfeld Panoramastrasse = Germany''s highest panoramic road (15.4 km, ~1,570 m crest, built 1937-40); year-round toll ~EUR 9/car"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 (fire + ambulance, EU) / 110 police; mountain rescue Bergwacht Bayern via 112","hospital":"Kreisklinik Berchtesgaden (local); serious cases Klinikum Traunstein","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"Watzmann + national park serious alpine terrain (accident-prone, whiteout, fast weather); Watzmann East Face (~1,800 m, longest wall in Eastern Alps) expert roped alpinists only; Jenner is freeride/ski-touring (not a controlled groomed resort) so avalanche bulletin is decisive — Lawinenwarndienst Bayern (lawinenwarndienst.bayern.de) publishes next-day forecast from 18:00 German+English, 5-level scale, 10 sub-regions; go guided + transceiver/probe/shovel, turn back on high-danger days; Kehlsteinhaus road closed all winter (avalanche, 3 m snowpack); Konigssee = calm crewed electric-boat lake (winter service to St. Bartholoma only, deep cold water); Obersee/Rothbachfall = long remote day, min